n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v & \\le 28 \\\\ 7\\cdot 3 & \\le 28 \\\\ 21 & \\le 28\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $v=3$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $v=3$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $v=4$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v & \\le 28 \\\\ 7\\cdot 4 & \\le 28 \\\\ 28 & \\le 28\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $v=4$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $v=4$ **satisfies** this inequality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068783 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fdde75-121e-5378-bad1-1ab564375d41" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values that Satisfy a Given Compound Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db1b76bd-cc4e-5494-bb2c-0ef5978d995e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067991} {:answer/id #uuid "eccebac7-1cc2-5ac8-8586-f1b4ba12efe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067992} {:answer/id #uuid "03eae620-0a72-5ac8-8c06-ed97d97ba78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067993} {:answer/id #uuid "0af28cfe-55f0-5316-a265-32fa7f9b5716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067994} {:answer/id #uuid "42d3994d-6cc2-58e9-94f1-8aa6404ab537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03eae620-0a72-5ac8-8c06-ed97d97ba78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067993} :answer-field/id #uuid "1045cfc3-db82-5ebf-9a58-ef4781fcdd16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cdbf09e-9c7d-57f8-ba2f-16618f332918" :question/math-academy-id "q-64151" :question/problem "Which of the following values of $a$ satisfy the inequality $-3\\le 2a+1<8\\,?$\n\nI. $a=-2$\n\nII. $a=2$\n\nIII. $a=5$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=-2$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot (-2)+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le -3 & <8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=-2$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=-2$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=2$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot 2+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 5 & <8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=2$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=2$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=5$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot 5+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 11 & <8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=5$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=5$ **does not satisfy** this inequality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd07be8d-2eba-5e4e-ba42-72470fd12120" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Inequalities that are Satisfied by a Given Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0eee43-3c3b-5cf1-b821-815de06c2e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483589} {:answer/id #uuid "7014de79-761f-5456-a6d2-f11d19d9da29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483786} {:answer/id #uuid "71830e5c-9c70-5069-8fa9-9cc06cc5361d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483790} {:answer/id #uuid "9e52646d-2f83-5953-bf3e-f68ff80dda37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483893} {:answer/id #uuid "a3bc4ed8-312a-5466-a03d-19b61f8cff89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e52646d-2f83-5953-bf3e-f68ff80dda37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483893} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa453620-268d-58a5-a4aa-728f054cf05d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed3aeee5-2189-5d52-8e31-431c161f29f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64157" :question/problem "The value $y=-1$ satisfies which of the following inequalities?\n\nI. $2<y+1<8$\n\nII. $4y<5$\n\nIII. $2\\le y+3$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute the given value into each of the inequalities and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the first inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2<y+1 & <8 \\\\ 2<-1+1 & <8 \\\\ 2<0 & <8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ ** does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the second inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & <5 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1) & <5 \\\\ -4 & <5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the third inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le y+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le -1+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le 2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ **satisfies** this inequality."}]}
